From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:40:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Skip useResource of buffer device address buffers with a
 residency set.

encodeGPUAddressableBuffers collects every buffer with a device address
for useResource, which runs only at the next draw. A buffer destroyed on
another thread in between leaves a dangling MTLBuffer there: useResources
then crashes in objc_msgSend or the command buffer fails with "Invalid
Resource". With a residency set the memory of these buffers is resident
already, so skip the list. vkd3d-proton, which uses buffer device
addresses throughout, hit this within seconds.

Also log whether resources are made resident through a residency set.
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
index 6fc4443..fc3924e 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
@@ -4601,6 +4601,11 @@ MVKBuffer* MVKDevice::removeBuffer(MVKBuffer* mvkBuff) {
 }
 
 void MVKDevice::encodeGPUAddressableBuffers(MVKUseResourceHelper& resources, MVKResourceUsageStages stage) {
+	// The residency set already holds the memory of these buffers. The list used here
+	// is handed to useResource only at the next draw, by when another thread may have
+	// destroyed a buffer, which faults in Metal or loses the device ("Invalid Resource").
+	if (hasResidencySet()) { return; }
+
 	lock_guard<mutex> lock(_rezLock);
 	for (auto& buff : _gpuAddressableBuffers) {
 		resources.add(buff->getMTLBuffer(), stage, true);
@@ -5466,6 +5471,7 @@ void MVKDevice::initQueues(const VkDeviceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo) {
 		[setDescriptor release];
 	}
 #endif
+	MVKLogInfo("Resources are made resident %s.", hasResidencySet() ? "through a residency set" : "with useResource per encoder");
 
 	auto qFams = _physicalDevice->getQueueFamilies();
 	uint32_t qrCnt = pCreateInfo->queueCreateInfoCount;
